For the owners of this classic Tacoma, Ark Splash Guards provide the solution for enhanced protection and style. They provide a cleaner, more professional look by covering gaps between the fenders and tires, which is especially important for trucks like the 1995-2004 Tacoma that may have seen years of service. Understanding the challenges these trucks face, especially when navigating rough terrains or city streets, our splash guards are designed to offer unparalleled resilience and coverage. They are specifically tailored to withstand the continuous impacts and debris encountered, preserving the truck's legendary durability and robustness.
Tailored Fit
Perfect fit for the various configurations of the 1995-2004 Tacoma, whether it's a two-door or four-door model, with different cab sizes and bed lengths. Our comprehensive range includes custom options for various suspension and body lifts, ensuring that every Tacoma owner, regardless of their truck’s specifics, can enjoy the benefits of our superior splash guards.
Easy Installation and Confidence in Quality
In line with our commitment to quality and customer satisfaction, Ark Splash Guards are designed for easy installation, providing straightforward instructions for a hassle-free setup. This ease of installation, combined with our 1 year, no-questions-asked refund policy, reflects our confidence in the American-made quality of our products and our dedication to delivering the best in protection, style, durability, and craftsmanship. With Ark Splash Guards, Tacoma owners can confidently tackle any adventure, knowing their vehicle is equipped with the best in protection and style.
Difference between Body Lifts and Suspension Lifts
Body Lift – A body lift raises the truck’s body away from the frame using spacers or blocks, typically providing 1 to 5 inches of height without altering the factory suspension. This method enhances aesthetics and allows for larger tires, but does not increase ground clearance. Since a body lift changes the geometry between the body and the frame, you’ll need to select the appropriate body lift height when ordering your Ark Splash Guards from our website to ensure a perfect fit.
Suspension Lift – A suspension lift raises the entire suspension system, including the frame, increasing ground clearance and improving off-road performance. Ranging from 2 to 9 inches (or more), this lift allows for larger tires and better handling on rugged terrain. Because a suspension lift does not alter the body-to-frame geometry, the Stock or Suspension Lift variant of Ark Splash Guards will fit seamlessly, regardless of your suspension lift height.

